# NODX Extended Showcase {#showcase-title .hero}

This document is intentionally richer than the minimal examples. It declares
style sheets, component manifests, local media assets, a public verification key,
signature placeholders, and agent change history while remaining readable as
plain text.

:::toc {#toc}
:::

::::section {#identity}
## Document Identity

:::note {#scope type="info"}
This is still a source document. The renderer may use styles from
`styles/editorial.nods` when bundled, but the semantic AST does not depend on
those presentation rules.
:::

:::table {#resource-table caption="Declared resource files"}
:::row
:::cell {header="true" scope="col"}
Resource
:::
:::cell {header="true" scope="col"}
Purpose
:::
:::
:::row
:::cell
styles/editorial.nods
:::
:::cell
Declarative style hints for headings, notes, tables, and custom components.
:::
:::
