::::

::::section {#custom-components}
## Custom Components

:::legal-clause {#legal-it jurisdiction="IT" fallback="children"}
The legal-clause component renders as ordinary text when unsupported. The
component manifest can add schema and rendering hints without changing the
fallback.
:::

:::approval-card {#approval release="{{vars.release}}" status="pending" fallback="children"}
Approval is pending security review. Agents must create a change record before
modifying this block.
:::

:::agent-review {#agent-findings sensitivity="internal" fallback="children"}
- [x] Stable IDs are present for critical sections
- [x] Unknown components preserve children
- [ ] Package signature is illustrative only
:::
::::

::::section {#media}
## Media And Embeds

:::figure {#fig-architecture}
:::image {src="assets/reference-pipeline.svg" alt="Pipeline diagram showing parser, validator, canonical AST, and renderers"}
:::
:::caption
Local SVG asset rendered by safe viewers or shown through fallback text.
:::
:::

:::media {#demo-video src="assets/demo-placeholder.txt" type="text/plain" alt="Demo transcript placeholder"}
Media playback is disabled by default. This fallback explains what a video or
audio renderer would expose in a safe host.
:::

:::embed {#external-report src="reports/compliance.pdf" type="application/pdf" alt="Compliance report"}
This embed points at a package-local report. Renderers that cannot display PDF
should keep this fallback.
:::
::::

::::section {#citations-and-breaks}
## Citations, Bibliography, And Print Hints

NODX supports citation references such as [@nodx-wd] and explicit page breaks.

:::pagebreak {#print-break}
:::

